1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,428
WenQuest's electronics track runs from a circuit, to a board, to a chip,

2
00:00:04,448 --> 00:00:06,237
and all the way into the factory.

3
00:00:07,257 --> 00:00:11,235
It starts with circuit analysis: build a circuit in the browser,

4
00:00:11,255 --> 00:00:12,172
change a value,

5
00:00:12,342 --> 00:00:14,525
and the simulation runs on the spot.

6
00:00:15,245 --> 00:00:18,618
Virtual instruments bring sensors, oscilloscopes and meters to the web,

7
00:00:18,788 --> 00:00:19,991
set up like real devices.

8
00:00:20,711 --> 00:00:22,258
Then a real joint drive board:

9
00:00:22,278 --> 00:00:25,653
the schematic and layout are generated from a design description,

10
00:00:26,673 --> 00:00:29,151
and you can compare revisions A and B side by side.

11
00:00:29,871 --> 00:00:32,965
Its firmware runs too, spinning a motor in a simulator:

12
00:00:33,135 --> 00:00:36,741
current loop, encoders, brake and protections, scenario by scenario.

13
00:00:37,461 --> 00:00:40,764
The encoder interface chip on that board is our own design too,

14
00:00:40,784 --> 00:00:42,927
from Verilog through synthesis to layout,

15
00:00:43,397 --> 00:00:45,042
all with open-source tools.

16
00:00:46,062 --> 00:00:49,633
The boards and chips then go into production and test in the digital

17
00:00:49,653 --> 00:00:51,745
factory's circuit board and chip plants,

18
00:00:51,915 --> 00:00:53,580
and on to the robot plant.

19
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:57,507
For companies there is WenQuest Electronics: AI drafts the design,

20
00:00:58,527 --> 00:01:02,925
and the factory checks incoming production files automatically and raises

21
00:01:02,945 --> 00:01:04,074
issues on the spot.

22
00:01:04,794 --> 00:01:07,992
You can open every one of them from "Electronics and chips" on our homepage.
